.TH PICSEL 1 2026-11-22 "picsel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
picsel \- choose which pictures of a folder to keep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B picsel
.RB [ \-\-resume =\fIwhen\fR]
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B picsel
.B \-\-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B picsel
shows the JPEG pictures and MP4/MOV videos of a folder as a mosaic. You
mark the ones to keep (or the ones to reject) with the keyboard, then press
.B Move
to move the selected files into a destination folder (by default, the
parent folder).
.PP
If
.I path
is a picture, picsel opens its folder with that picture highlighted, unless
the folder remembers another one (see below). If it is a folder, or the
.I picsel.db
file of a folder, picsel opens that folder. Without
.IR path ,
picsel asks for a folder. If picsel is already running, the folder opens in
the running instance.
.PP
The first time a folder is opened, picsel asks for the destination folder
and for whether pictures start as selected or not selected. Every change is
saved immediately, so you can quit and continue later. Files added, removed
or renamed while picsel runs are picked up automatically.
.PP
Closing a folder's window remembers the highlighted picture, and by default
the folder reopens there, even when it is opened through another picture.
A remembered picture renamed while picsel was closed is followed; if it is
gone, the picture now in its place is highlighted, unless a picture was
given. The
.B Reopen at
setting in the side panel, or
.BR \-\-resume ,
changes this.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check that the Qt modules, plugins and codecs picsel needs at run time are
installed, print a report and exit. The exit status is 1 if picsel cannot
start; missing video codecs only affect videos.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume= when
Where the folder starts, for this launch only (it overrides the side panel's
.B Reopen at
setting).
.B always
(the default) starts at the picture highlighted when the folder was last
closed, even if
.I path
is another picture;
.B folder
does so only when
.I path
is a folder, and starts at the given picture otherwise;
.B never
starts at the given picture or at the first one, like picsel 0.1.0.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR S " / " D
Select / deselect the current picture, then go to the next one.
.TP
.B T
Toggle the selection without moving.
.TP
.B Arrows
Move around (left and right wrap across rows).
.TP
.BR Home " / " End ", " PgUp " / " PgDn
First / last picture, page up / down.
.TP
.BR Enter " or double click"
Full view (Esc or Enter closes it).
.TP
.BR Space " / " M
In the full view, play or pause a video / toggle its sound.
.TP
.BR + " / " \-
Bigger / smaller thumbnails.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo selection changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I picsel.db
Per-folder state (selection, destination, the picture highlighted at the
last close), kept inside the opened folder.
.TP
.I ~/.config/picsel/picsel.ini
Global settings, such as camera clock corrections and where folders reopen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PICSEL_STANDALONE
If set, do not hand the folder to a running instance and do not accept
folders from later launches.
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME
If unset, picsel uses Qt's
.B xdgdesktopportal
theme, so folder dialogs are the desktop's own, shown through the XDG
desktop portal. Set it to choose another Qt platform theme.
.TP
.B QT_FFMPEG_DEBUG
If set, keep the full log of Qt's ffmpeg media backend, which picsel
otherwise quietens.
.SH NOTES
picsel is Linux-only: it follows folder changes with inotify.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/rg3/picsel
